data live_tree_disposition: LiveTreeDisposition = ReadsLiveTree

// XL-3 WAVE 2, UNRUN -- written and pinned at origin/main 345d6077fc4a, never executed. The shape is
// wave 1's (src/v2/test/claim/long/xl3_wave_declaring_identity_witness.dag on this branch): a pinned
// table keyed by DECLARING PATH with an occurrence count, one native front end and one resolution per
// subject module, and a wrong-declaration arm that must REFUSE. Wave 1 is the authority for the shape;
// this file does not fork it -- it imports ExpectedBinding, read_of, declaring_paths and table_holds.
//
// SCOPE (tidy-ant-251 ruling): wave 2 touches the importers of std.declaring_identity_spelling, and an
// import edit can change what an UNCHANGED spelling resolves to. So each table below pins EVERY
// reference in the touched module that an import row gives a home to -- not only the references to
// std.declaring_identity_spelling. Same-module references, binder-bound positions and record field
// labels are listed in docs/plans/2026-11-01-xl3-wave2-declaring-identity-references.md and are NOT
// pinned here, with the reason stated there.
//
// COUNTS are non-comment, non-import mentions by `git grep -w` reading at 345d6077fc4a (commands,
// population and unknowns in the note); they are UNVERIFIED against the resolver until the first run,
// which may correct a count (an unread arm of a record, a mention the resolver does not mint). The
// first run is EXPECTED to refuse before any count is read: production_ingest.dag:80 still calls the
// unbound `filesystem_read`, and every subject's closure reaches src/v2/std/qualified_name.dag, which
// calls the unbound `string_length` (line 304) until #15507 lands. Both are named in the note.

// SUBJECT v2.compiler.declaring_identity_spelling_census  (src/v2/compiler/declaring_identity_spelling_census.dag): 36 import-row references, 47 occurrences,
